{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771168456197,"sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","part":{"id":"prt_c61ddddd80014eYiYTzTJH51Gh","sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","messageID":"msg_c61ddc64e001HMDy3C3Xb7P7Vk","type":"tool","callID":"call_8772c2a85bca4c8fa639d9f4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/flux-management.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/flux-management.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Flux Management\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Resource management system for strategic cell placement. Players have a limited pool of \"Flux\" to place cells during both PLANNING and PLAYING phases. Flux can be saved during planning for use during play phase.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Core Mechanics\n9: - **Initial Allocation**: Each level starts with 20 Flux (configurable via expert settings, range: 5-50)\n10: - **Placement Cost**: Each cell placed costs exactly 1 Flux (same cost in both phases)\n11: - **Refund Mechanic**: Clicking an existing cell during PLANNING phase removes it and refunds 1 Flux (full refund)\n12: - **No Refunds in Play Phase**: Cells placed during RUNNING phase cannot be removed\n13: - **Zero State**: When Flux reaches 0, placement is disabled with visual/audio feedback\n14: - **Strategic Choice**: Players decide how much Flux to use during planning vs save for play phase\n15: \n16: ### State Management\n17: ```typescript\n18: interface FluxState {\n19:   current: number;           // Available Flux\n20:   initial: number;           // Starting amount for level\n21:   placed: number;            // Total cells placed (for stats)\n22:   removed: number;          // Total cells removed (for stats)\n23: }\n24: ```\n25: \n26: ### Validation Rules\n27: - Cannot place cell if Flux < 1\n28: - Cannot place cell outside grid bounds\n29: - Refund only applies during PLANNING phase\n30: - No refunds during RUNNING or FINISHED phases\n31: - Can place cells during RUNNING phase using saved Flux\n32: - No remove functionality during RUNNING phase (add-only)\n33: \n34: ## UI/UX Requirements\n35: \n36: ### HUD Display\n37: - **Location**: Bottom center of screen\n38: - **Visual**: Bar or counter showing current/initial\n39: - **Color Coding**:\n40:    - Green/Yellow when plenty remaining\n41:    - Orange when < 30% remaining\n42:    - Red when 0 remaining\n43: - **Animation**: Smooth transitions when values change\n44: - **Phase Indication**: Always visible in both PLANNING and RUNNING phases\n45: \n46: ### Feedback\n47: - **Insufficient Resources**: \n48:   - Audio: Error/denied sound\n49:   - Visual: Brief red flash on Flux counter\n50: - **Placement**: \n51:   - Audio: Soft \"plop\" sound\n52:   - Visual: Cell appears with fade-in animation\n53: - **Removal**: \n54:   - Audio: Suction/remove sound\n55:   - Visual: Cell shrinks and disappears\n56: \n57: ## Edge Cases\n58: \n59: 1. **Zero Flux at Start**: If initial Flux is 0, game should warn or prevent level start\n60: 2. **Accidental Removal**: User might misclick during planning - no undo needed since they can just place again\n61: 3. **Lag Between Click and Update**: Ensure Flux decrement is atomic with cell placement to prevent race conditions\n62: 4. **Strategic Decisions**: Players must balance using Flux in planning vs saving for play phase\n63: 5. **Play Phase Placement**: Must coordinate with simulation step to prevent race conditions\n64: \n65: ## Implementation Notes\n66: \n67: - Store Flux in React state (useState or useReducer)\n68: - Flux changes should be logged for analytics/debugging\n69: - Consider debouncing rapid clicks to prevent accidental over-spending\n70: - Mobile: Ensure touch targets are large enough to prevent misclicks\n71: - Play phase placement must use timing coordination with simulation step\n72: - Queue placements if player clicks mid-simulation step\n73: - Flux counter resets every level (no carryover between levels)\n74: \n75: \n\n(End of file - total 75 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/flux-management.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Flux Management\n\n## Overview\nResource management system for strategic cell placement. Players have a limited pool of \"Flux\" to place cells during both PLANNING and PLAYING phases. Flux can be saved during planning for use during play phase.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Core Mechanics\n- **Initial Allocation**: Each level starts with 20 Flux (configurable via expert settings, range: 5-50)\n- **Placement Cost**: Each cell placed costs exactly 1 Flux (same cost in both phases)\n- **Refund Mechanic**: Clicking an existing cell during PLANNING phase removes it and refunds 1 Flux (full refund)\n- **No Refunds in Play Phase**: Cells placed during RUNNING phase cannot be removed\n- **Zero State**: When Flux reaches 0, placement is disabled with visual/audio feedback\n- **Strategic Choice**: Players decide how much Flux to use during planning vs save for play phase\n\n### State Management\n```typescript\ninterface FluxState {\n  current: number;           // Available Flux\n  initial: number;           // Starting amount for level","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771168456161,"end":1771168456194}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771168456201,"sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","part":{"id":"prt_c61dddde5001uzpflEDdGfv86t","sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","messageID":"msg_c61ddc64e001HMDy3C3Xb7P7Vk","type":"tool","callID":"call_d1066ea40a68475e83439ee3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Grid Interaction\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Direct manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n9: - **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n10: - **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n11: - **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n12: - **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n13: \n14: ### Interaction Constraints\n15: - Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n16: - Disabled during FINISHED phase\n17: - Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n18: - Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n19: \n20: ### Coordinate System\n21: ```typescript\n22: interface GridInteraction {\n23:   cellX: number;        // 0 to gridWidth-1\n24:   cellY: number;        // 0 to gridHeight-1\n25:   isPlaceable: boolean; // Calculated based on Flux and existing cell\n26: }\n27: ```\n28: \n29: ## UI/UX Requirements\n30: \n31: ### Cursor States\n32: - **Default**: Standard cursor\n33: - **Over Empty Cell (Placeable)**: Crosshair or cell preview outline\n34: - **Over Empty Cell (Unplaceable)**: Forbidden symbol (Flux = 0)\n35: - **Over Live Cell (Removable)**: Minus icon or highlight\n36: \n37: ### Visual Feedback\n38: - **Cell Preview**: Ghost/outline of cell follows cursor when hovering over grid\n39: - **Cell Placement**: Fade-in animation (0.1s duration)\n40: - **Cell Removal**: Shrink animation (0.15s duration)\n41: - **Invalid Action**: Brief red flash on cursor location\n42: \n43: ### Mobile Considerations\n44: - Pinch-to-zoom disabled on game grid\n45: - Touch-and-hold to drag not needed (single click only)\n46: - Prevent accidental browser zoom on double-tap\n47: - Visual ripple effect on touch\n48: \n49: ## Edge Cases\n50: \n51: 1. **Rapid Clicking**: User might click faster than animation - ensure state consistency\n52: 2. **Edge of Grid**: Clicking exactly on grid boundary should round to nearest cell\n53: 3. **Overlapping with UI**: Ensure grid doesn't extend under HUD elements\n54: 4. **Window Resize**: Grid cells must maintain aspect ratio on resize\n55: \n56: ## Implementation Notes\n57: \n58: - Use event delegation for grid click handling\n59: - Calculate cell coordinates from mouse/touch position: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n60: - Consider using CSS Grid or Canvas for rendering - Canvas may be better for performance with many cells\n61: - Implement hit testing to distinguish between grid cells and gaps\n62: \n\n(End of file - total 62 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/grid-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Grid Interaction\n\n## Overview\nDirect manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n- **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n- **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n- **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n- **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n\n### Interaction Constraints\n- Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n- Disabled during FINISHED phase\n- Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n- Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n\n### Coordinate System","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771168456168,"end":1771168456198}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771168456204,"sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","part":{"id":"prt_c61ddddca0011rg37xRpeVD1yo","sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","messageID":"msg_c61ddc64e001HMDy3C3Xb7P7Vk","type":"tool","callID":"call_1256b516c87c431086251a4a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: User Interaction System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Interaction Modes\n9: ```typescript\n10: type InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n11: ```\n12: \n13: **Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n14: **Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n15: \n16: ### Mouse Interaction\n17: \n18: #### Mouse Down\n19: 1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n20: 2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n21: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n22: \n23: #### Mouse Move (while pressed)\n24: 1. Capture mouse position\n25: 2. Convert to grid coordinates\n26: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n27: \n28: #### Mouse Up (global)\n29: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n30: 2. Prevent stale drag state\n31: \n32: ### Touch Interaction\n33: \n34: #### Touch Start\n35: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n36: 2. Capture first touch position\n37: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n38: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n39: \n40: #### Touch Move\n41: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n42: 2. Capture first touch position\n43: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n44: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n45: \n46: #### Touch End / Cancel\n47: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n48: \n49: ## Implementation Architecture\n50: \n51: ### Coordinate Mapping\n52: ```typescript\n53: interface GridCoordinates {\n54:   row: number; // 0 to numRows-1\n55:   col: number; // 0 to numCols-1\n56: }\n57: \n58: function getCellFromEvent(\n59:   event: MouseEvent | TouchEvent,\n60:   canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\n61:   numRows: number,\n62:   numCols: number\n63: ): GridCoordinates\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ### Interaction Handler\n67: ```typescript\n68: function handleCellInteract(\n69:   row: number,\n70:   col: number,\n71:   type: 'down' | 'enter'\n72: ): void\n73: ```\n74: \n75: - **type='down'**: Modify cell(s)\n76: - **type='enter'**: Only modify if mouse down\n77: \n78: ### Sound Integration\n79: - **Draw/Erase**: Play interaction sound (different tones)\n80: - **Sound Engine**: Called per cell interaction\n81: \n82: ## Edge Cases\n83: \n84: 1. **Boundary Coordinates**: Math.floor() ensures valid indices\n85: 2. **Rapid Clicking**: Multiple clicks allowed\n86: 3. **Canvas Resize**: Grid dimensions update, coordinates recalculate\n87: 4. **Touch Conflicts**: PreventDefault() blocks browser zoom/scroll\n88: 5. **Mouse Leave Canvas**: Set isMouseDown to false to stop drag\n89: \n90: ## Mobile Considerations\n91: \n92: - **Touch Action**: `touch-action: none` on canvas element\n93: - **Target Size**: Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop) meets minimum touch target\n94: - **Prevent Default**: Stop scrolling while drawing\n95: - **Multi-touch**: Only first touch used (ignore additional touches)\n96: \n97: ## Visual Feedback\n98: \n99: - **Cursor**: `crosshair` style over canvas\n100: - **Hover Effects**: None (draw directly on grid)\n101: - **Selection Feedback**: No preview shown (immediate drawing)\n102: \n103: ## Dependencies\n104: \n105: - Core simulation engine: Grid ref and dimensions\n106: - Audio sonification system: Play interaction sounds\n107: - Canvas rendering system: Redraw on state change\n108: \n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/user-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: User Interaction System\n\n## Overview\nThe user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Interaction Modes\n```typescript\ntype InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n```\n\n**Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n**Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n### Mouse Interaction\n\n#### Mouse Down\n1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771168456146,"end":1771168456202}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771168456208,"sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","part":{"id":"prt_c61ddddae001WomGi4A3ScTbIL","sessionID":"ses_39e2260a5ffeBhM9ggj7NVvnno","messageID":"msg_c61ddc64e001HMDy3C3Xb7P7Vk","type":"tool","callID":"call_159252134676420781843da7","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Canvas Rendering System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The canvas rendering system draws the Game of Life grid with age-based neon color gradients and glow effects using HTML5 Canvas for high-performance rendering.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Rendering Theme\n9: **Dark Neon Theme**:\n10: - Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n11: - Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, only during PLANNING phase)\n12: \n13: **Cell Age-Based Colors**:\n14: - Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan, intense glow)\n15: - Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue, medium glow)\n16: - Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink, subtle glow)\n17: - Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple, minimal glow)\n18: \n19: **Glow Effects**:\n20: - Age 0: Shadow blur = 15px (highly visible)\n21: - Age 1-2: Shadow blur = 8px\n22: - Age 3-5: Shadow blur = 4px\n23: - Age 6+: Shadow blur = 2px\n24: \n25: ### Cell Rendering\n26: - **Cell Size**: Responsive (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n27: - **Age-Based Colors**: Color computed from cell state value\n28: - **Glow Effects**: Shadow blur and shadow color applied\n29: - **Shape**: Square with slight corner radius (2px)\n30: \n31: ### Grid Lines\n32: - **Visibility**: Toggleable (keyboard shortcut: 'G' key), only shown when not running\n33: - **Color**: `#1a1a2e` (subtle)\n34: - **Stroke Width**: 1px\n35: - **Position**: Around each cell\n36: - **Default**: Hidden during RUNNING phase, visible during PLANNING phase\n37: \n38: ## Implementation Architecture\n39: \n40: ### Canvas Setup\n41: ```typescript\n42: interface CanvasConfig {\n43:   width: number;  // numCols * cellSize\n44:   height: number; // numRows * cellSize\n45:   dpr: number;   // window.devicePixelRatio\n46:   cellSize: number; // 18px (mobile) or 20px (desktop)\n47: }\n48: ```\n49: \n50: ### Responsive Cell Sizing\n51: - Mobile devices (screen width < 768px): 18px cells\n52: - Desktop devices (screen width >= 768px): 20px cells\n53: - Cell size updates on window resize\n54: - Grid dimensions recalculate based on cell size\n55: \n56: ### Rendering Pipeline\n57: 1. **Canvas Resize**: Update width/height if dimensions changed\n58: 2. **Transform Reset**: Clear and apply DPR scaling\n59: 3. **Draw Loop**:\n60:    - Clear canvas with background color\n61:    - Draw grid lines (if enabled)\n62:    - Draw live cells with age-based styling and glow\n63: 4. **Intensity Update**: Set CSS variable `--life-intensity`\n64: \n65: ### Performance Optimizations\n66: - **DPR Scaling**: Use `window.devicePixelRatio` for sharp rendering\n67: - **Transform Reset**: Clear transform before resize\n68: - **Optimized Draws**: Minimize context state changes\n69: - **Dependency Tracking**: useCallback on [numRows, numCols, cellSize]\n70: \n71: ## Visual Effects\n72: \n73: ### Glow/Shadows\n74: ```typescript\n75: interface CellShadow {\n76:   blur: number;    // 2px to 15px based on age\n77:   color: string;  // Matches cell color\n78: }\n79: ```\n80: \n81: ### Intensity Metric\n82: ```typescript\n83: const intensity = Math.min(activeCount / 500, 1);\n84: document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--life-intensity', intensity.toString());\n85: ```\n86: - Used for CSS-based ambient effects\n87: - Scaled from 0-500 cells\n88: \n89: ## Edge Cases\n90: \n91: 1. **Canvas Resize**: Must handle width/height update, DPR scaling, and cell size recalculation together\n92: 2. **Empty Grid**: Draws only grid lines (if enabled)\n93: 3. **High Cell Count**: May have performance issues with 500+ cells\n94: 4. **Rapid Cell Size Changes**: Color computations cached per frame\n95: \n96: ## Mobile Considerations\n97: \n98: - Touch coordinates mapped to canvas space\n99: - Prevent browser zoom on canvas interaction\n100: - Maintain 18px cell size on mobile\n101: - Ensure minimum 10 cells visible in smallest dimension\n102: \n103: ## Dependencies\n104: \n105: - Core simulation engine: Provides grid state and dimensions\n106: - UI/overlay system: Grid line toggle setting\n107: - User interaction system: Triggers redraws on cell changes\n108: \n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/canvas-rendering.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Canvas Rendering System\n\n## Overview\nThe canvas rendering system draws the Game of Life grid with age-based neon color gradients and glow effects using HTML5 Canvas for high-performance rendering.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Rendering Theme\n**Dark Neon Theme**:\n- Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n- Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, only during PLANNING phase)\n\n**Cell Age-Based Colors**:\n- Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan, intense glow)\n- Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue, medium glow)\n- Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink, subtle glow)\n- Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple, minimal glow)\n\n**Glow Effects**:\n- Age 0: Shadow blur = 15px (highly visible)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771168456129,"end":1771168456205}}}}
